    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d580">

                <pb facs="0578" n="480" sameAs="frus:frus1900/pg480"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Porter.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-10-23"><hi rendition="#italic">October 23,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 839.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I inclose for your information copy of a
                    dispatch from the consul of the United States at Havre, reporting the recent
                    death by drowning of Howard Linwood Ridlon, and stating that the French
                    officials promptly acceded to the request for permission to land a firing party
                    from the <hi rendition="#italic">Hartford</hi>, and that a delegation of French
                    soldiers was sent to the funeral.</p>
                <p>At the instance of the Secretary of the Navy, you are requested to convey to the
                    French Government the thanks of the Navy Department, in suitable terms, for the
                    courtesies of the former on the occasion.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>




                <xi:include href="d580-a1.xml" xpointer="d580-a1"/>
